# Prefer UFCS

In `.ccs` / `.cch` call sites, **always prefer UFCS** over the free-function form of the same API.

```ccs
// prefer
db.maps.count();
maps->hold_one(si);
hold.release();
sh->get(key);
c->lit("$-1\r\n");

// avoid (same APIs)
cc_shard_map_count(&db.maps);
cc_shard_map_hold_one(maps, si);
cc_shard_hold_release(&hold);
cc_shard_get(sh, key);
conn_lit(c, "$-1\r\n");
```

Use a local pointer when peel drops `&` on `ptr->field.meth()`:

```ccs
CCShardMap* maps = &db->maps;
maps->shard(si);
maps->init(excl, mask);
```

For value locals, dot UFCS is preferred (`db.maps.count()`, `maps.destroy()`). Prefer that over `cc_shard_map_*` free calls.

Free-function names are for lowered/host C and definitions — not the surface idiom in sketches and examples.
